**Why it failed:** No compile or correctness error — `correct: true`, max_abs_err ≤ 0.00177 vs threshold 0.0147. Performance did not improve: aggregate score stayed at 2.939 (per-config ~3.02 TFLOPs). No committed improvement; the scalar Q·K dot-product loop and column-wise online softmax remain dominant, so load/exp2 tweaks are second-order.

**Avoid / retry differently:** Don't keep tuning the same path. Profile first to confirm the bottleneck, then attack the scalar dot product (ldmatrix for Q/K tiles, register blocking across rows, cp.async) or reduce softmax/online-update overhead. GQA code is correct but untested with kv_heads < heads (eval used kv_heads=16 = heads).

